knext bundled fix for vinext 1.0.1 (dist output)
Upstream: https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/pull/3686
What it fixes: next/image's image optimizer path ignored `trailingSlash: true`
(always emitted `/_next/image?...`, never `/_next/image/?...`), and a custom
`loader` prop was called once at the intrinsic width with quality forced to
75 -- producing no `srcSet` and overriding the loader's own quality default.
This patch fixes the trailingSlash path and gives a custom loader the same
per-breakpoint srcSet treatment as the built-in loader, passing `quality`
through as given (including undefined) rather than forcing 75.
Scope note: the upstream PR also wires up `images.loaderFile` (previously
ignored entirely) via a build-time resolve.alias entry in index.ts; that
part is NOT bundled here because it would add a cross-module import this
dist file cannot resolve outside vinext's own Vite plugin pipeline, and is
better delivered as a small, separate dist/index.js patch once proven.
`images.loaderFile` remains ignored until the upstream release; the `loader`
prop fix above is independent of it and fully bundled.
Retire: delete this file (and its manifest entry) when the pinned vinext is >= the first
release that includes cloudflare/vinext#3686.
Ported by hand from the upstream src change to the published 1.0.1 dist files.
Applied by `knext vinext-patches` (runs from the app's postinstall and before `knext build`).

